  <item>
    <title>97. 如何用ABM理解结婚和生育决策？</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/6a1a41c2ac7bdb080c330027</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">6a1a41c2ac7bdb080c330027</guid>
    <pubDate>Sat, 30 May 2026 01:51:59 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>本期播客介绍了Agent-based Modeling基于主体建模的方法，以及如何用ABM来理解结婚和生育决策。</span></p><p><strong><span>【本期主播】</span></strong></p><p><span>晓昕</span></p><p><strong><span>【收听指南】</span></strong></p><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="60">01:00</a> ABM的定义</span></p><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="105">01:45</a> 谢林隔离模型</span></p><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="318">05:18</a> 设计效用函数</span></p><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="488">08:08</a> LLM+ABM</span></p><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="668">11:08</a> 婚育决策模型</span></p><p><strong><span>【参考文献】</span></strong></p><p><span>Bertrand, M., Goldin, C., &amp; Katz, L. F. (2010). Dynamics of the gender gap for young professionals in the financial and corporate sectors. </span><em><span>American Economic Journal: Applied Economics</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>2</span></em><span>(3), 228–255.</span></p><p><span>Gao, C., et al. (2024). Large language models empowered agent-based modeling and simulation: A survey and perspectives. </span><em><span>Humanities and Social Sciences Communications</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>11</span></em><span>, 1259.</span></p><p><span>Goldin, C. (2014). A grand gender convergence: Its last chapter. </span><em><span>American Economic Review</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>104</span></em><span>(4), 1091–1119.</span></p><p><span>Kazil, J., Masad, D., &amp; Crooks, A. (2020). Utilizing Python for agent-based modeling: The Mesa framework. In R. Thomson et al. (Eds.), </span><em><span>Social, cultural, and behavioral modeling</span></em><span> (Lecture Notes in Computer Science, pp. 308–317). Springer International Publishing.</span></p><p><span>Kleven, H., Landais, C., &amp; Søgaard, J. E. (2019). Children and gender inequality: Evidence from Denmark. </span><em><span>American Economic Journal: Applied Economics</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>11</span></em><span>(4), 181–209.</span></p><p><span>Marwal, A., &amp; Silva, E. A. (2023). City affordability and residential location choice: A demonstration using agent-based model. </span><em><span>Habitat International</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>136</span></em><span>, 1–9.</span></p><p><span>O'Gara, D., et al. (2023). TRACE-Omicron: Policy counterfactuals to inform mitigation of COVID-19 spread in the United States. </span><em><span>Advanced Theory and Simulation</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>6</span></em><span>(7).</span></p><p><span>Park, J. S., O'Brien, J., Cai, C. J., Morris, M. R., Liang, P., &amp; Bernstein, M. S. (2023). Generative agents: Interactive simulacra of human behavior. In </span><em><span>Proceedings of the 36th Annual ACM Symposium on User Interface Software and Technology</span></em><span> (pp. 1–22). ACM.</span></p><p><span>Schelling, T. C. (1969). Models of segregation. </span><em><span>American Economic Review</span></em><span>, </span><em><span>59</span></em><span>(2), 488–493.</span></p><p></p>]]></description>
